{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Behold, a nation you do not know.</b> A nation you did not know you will call, that it may come to you, like the sense of for my servant I called (Job 19:16)." "<b>To you they will run.</b> Now what I interpreted is confirmed." "<b>Your glory (פארך).</b> An unusual word in grammar, for there is none like it among complete verbs, only among quiescent [letters], like your answer (ענך) (Isaiah 30:19)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:37.859860894Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}